<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Ch02_P02_Change_the_picture</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The same idea works with a bigger square cut from the corner. Start with a square of side \(x\) and cut a square of side {@cc@} from one corner.</p>
<p>(a) The strip along the top is {@cc@} high. How long is it?</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) After the strip is moved to the side, the pieces form a rectangle. Write its area as a product of two factors.</p>
<div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Complete the condition: the picture can be drawn exactly when</p>
<div>\(x \gt\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>Type products with <code>*</code>, for example <code>2*(x+3)</code>.</p>]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The method is the same as in the picture proof: cut a strip, move it, and compare areas.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The square has area \(x^2\). Cutting a {@cc@} by {@cc@} square from the corner leaves area \({@dexp@}\).</p></li>
<li><p>The strip along the top is \(x - {@cc@}\) long and {@cc@} high.</p></li>
<li><p>Moved to the side, it makes a rectangle \(x + {@cc@}\) long and \(x - {@cc@}\) high.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>So \({@dexp@} = (x + {@cc@})(x - {@cc@})\). The picture needs \(x - {@cc@} \gt 0\), that is \(x \gt {@cc@}\). Multiplying out \((x + {@cc@})(x - {@cc@})\) proves the same identity for every real number \(x\).</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
